PhoneNumberMetadata.xml — provenance and attribution
=====================================================

The metadata generator (generate.ae) reads the XML at the repository's own
canonical location:

    resources/PhoneNumberMetadata.xml

That file IS Google libphonenumber's authoritative metadata — this repository
is a fork of google/libphonenumber, so the file is already present and
maintained upstream. The Aether port does NOT vendor a second copy; it compiles
the in-tree one into core/metadata.ae.

  Source:  https://github.com/google/libphonenumber
  File:    resources/PhoneNumberMetadata.xml
  Format:  see resources/phonemetadata.proto for the schema the XML mirrors

License
-------
libphonenumber is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
Copyright (C) 2009 The Libphonenumber Authors.

The file retains its own Apache-2.0 copyright header (see the top of the XML
itself). The full license text is the repository's LICENSE (Apache-2.0).

libphonenumber ships NO NOTICE file, so Apache-2.0 section 4(d) imposes no
additional notice-carrying obligation. This PROVENANCE file records where the
generator's input comes from and what fraction of it the Aether port consumes.

What the generator consumes
---------------------------
Per territory: id, country calling code, the possible-lengths union
(isPossibleNumber), an example number, one display format (pattern + template),
the generalDesc national-number pattern, and the per-type national-number
patterns (fixedLine, mobile, tollFree, premiumRate, sharedCost, voip,
personalNumber, pager, uan, voicemail) — enough for isPossibleNumber,
isValidNumber, getNumberType and a national/international/E.164 formatter.

NOT consumed: leadingDigits routing between multiple <numberFormat> entries
(only the first format is captured as a display hint), carrier/geocoding
metadata (separate XML files), and the alternate-formats and short-number
metadata. Extending the generator to carry these needs no new fetch — the whole
XML is already in-tree.

ShortNumberMetadata.xml (ShortNumberInfo side-library)
-------------------------------------------------------
core/gen/generate_short.ae reads the in-tree resources/ShortNumberMetadata.xml
(Google's own, Apache-2.0) and compiles a subset into core/shortnumber_metadata.ae:
per territory, the generalDesc pattern, the shortCode pattern + possible-lengths,
an example, and the per-category national-number patterns (tollFree, premiumRate,
standardRate, carrierSpecific, smsServices, emergency). Enough for isValid/
isPossibleShortNumber, getExpectedCost, isEmergencyNumber, connectsToEmergencyNumber,
isCarrierSpecific, isSmsServiceForRegion. Pristine file, read directly, unmodified.

timezones/map_data.txt (PhoneNumberToTimeZonesMapper side-library)
------------------------------------------------------------------
core/gen/generate_tz.ae reads the in-tree resources/timezones/map_data.txt
(Google's own, Apache-2.0) — one "prefix|tz1&tz2&..." entry per line — and
compiles it verbatim into core/timezone_metadata.ae (3290 prefix entries). The
engine does a longest-prefix match over the E.164 digits. Pristine file, read
directly, unmodified.

carrier/en/<cc>.txt (PhoneNumberToCarrierMapper side-library)
-------------------------------------------------------------
core/gen/generate_carrier.ae reads the in-tree resources/carrier/en/<cc>.txt
files (Google's own, Apache-2.0) — one "prefix|CarrierName" entry per line, the
prefix being cc-inclusive E.164 digits — and compiles the ENGLISH names into
core/carrier_metadata.ae as a single newline-joined string blob (~29k entries;
too many for the compiler's per-function statement cap as list.add calls, fine
as one string constant). Longest-prefix match. Only the English (en/) slice is
carried; other languages can be added the same way. Pristine files, read
directly, unmodified.
